# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# `text=auto` lets Git decide text vs. binary per file and normalize line
# endings to LF in the repository (working-tree behavior still follows the
# user's core.autocrlf). The explicit rules below pin LF for every source
# and text file type actually used in this repo, regardless of local
# core.autocrlf settings, so history stays consistent across contributors.
#
# No Windows-specific script files (.ps1, .bat, .cmd) currently exist in
# this repository, so no CRLF override is defined. If one is ever added,
# give it an explicit `text eol=crlf` rule here rather than falling back to
# the auto default.

* text=auto

*.js  text eol=lf
*.jsx text eol=lf
*.ts  text eol=lf
*.tsx text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md  text eol=lf
*.sql text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
